<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>netstandard2.0</TargetFramework>
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
    <Authors>Vivelin</Authors>
    <Company>Decos Information Solutions</Company>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/DecosInformationSolutions/HttpSignatures</PackageProjectUrl>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <Description>A .NET Standard 2.0 library for validating signatures. Typically, the AuthenticationBuilder extension AddSignature would be used to add an ASP.NET Core authentication handler that authenticates requests with a valid signature.</Description>
    <Version>3.0.0</Version>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>
Security release. Contains a breaking change to signature validation.

- Validation is now bound to the scheme and host of the request. Both validation candidates include
  the authority, so a signature covering only the path is rejected rather than preferred.
  BREAKING: clients that sign a relative URI are no longer authenticated. Signers and validators
  must be upgraded together.
- A request without a Host header is rejected, because there is nothing to bind the signature to.
- Host binding depends on the application's forwarded-header configuration. Behind a reverse proxy,
  restrict ForwardedHeaders trust to known proxies and networks, otherwise the host a signature is
  bound to can be chosen by the caller.
    </PackageReleaseNotes>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Decos.Http.Signatures\Decos.Http.Signatures.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <Compile Update="Strings.Designer.cs">
      <DependentUpon>Strings.resx</DependentUpon>
      <DesignTime>True</DesignTime>
      <AutoGen>True</AutoGen>
    </Compile>
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <EmbeddedResource Update="Strings.resx">
      <LastGenOutput>Strings.Designer.cs</LastGenOutput>
      <Generator>ResXFileCodeGenerator</Generator>
    </EmbeddedResource>
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authentication" Version="2.2.0" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
